{"ts":"2026-07-30T22:37:52.785Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"7af60c336d5bedfb02d08cad","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-vcs-9c77"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Content-addressed object store: blobs, trees, commits and records"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Four object kinds framed as '<type> <byteLength>\\0<payload>' and addressed by SHA-256 over the whole frame, so identical content always yields an identical id. Blobs hold bytes, trees hold sorted (mode, name, id) entries, commits hold a tree plus zero or more parents with author and message, and records hold a structured document as canonically ordered fields - the kind that makes per-field merging possible. Loose objects are zlib-deflated and written through a temp file plus rename so a torn write can never leave a half object under a valid id."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:vcs"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-30T22:37:52.785Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-30T22:37:52.785Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Round-tripping any object of any kind returns byte-identical content; the same content written twice produces one object and one id; a corrupted payload is detected on read rather than returned; concurrent writers of the same object cannot observe a partial file"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"6a85bf06b873845cf3e3b273e6856fc11c9405d109617c125c7cbd6c2d459653","message":""}
